WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.350
Step into a gurdwara kitchen.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.440
Volunteers chop, stir and serve
free food to anyone who comes.

3
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:13.020
Others scrub the pots, sweep the floor,
or wipe the shoes of pilgrims at the door.

4
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.730
Guru Nanak taught: serve in this world,
and you will be given a seat of honour

5
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.420
in God's court.

6
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:24.220
So why would Sikhs say that washing
dishes can bring them closer to God?

7
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.670
In this mission, you'll sort Sikh service,

8
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.990
called sewa, into three
forms: body, mind and wealth.

9
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.300
Then you'll see how a prayer
said in every gurdwara,

10
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:39.150
for the welfare of all,
is meant to become action.

11
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: find out why Sikhs say
washing dishes can bring them closer to God.
